msgid "Classification mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "Traditional priority (default)"
msgstr ""

msgid "DSCP determines hardware queues"
msgstr ""

msgid "Traditional mode maps Linux priority to three QDMA classes: interactive/control, ordinary, and bulk/filler. PPE retains its existing TOS input; different forwarding paths may classify differently."
msgstr ""

msgid "DSCP mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "DSCP directly selects Q0–Q7 across CPU, PPE and switch paths. This avoids legacy TOS classification, stale skb priority and software-flowtable differences. The original skb priority is preserved, but does not choose the hardware queue for parsed IP packets. Mark traffic consistently in both directions before offload; established PPE flows do not follow per-packet DSCP changes."
msgstr ""

msgid "DSCP → queue overrides"
msgstr ""

msgid "Format DSCP:QUEUE. Unspecified values retain the original PPE numeric map; this is not a standard DiffServ/WMM mapping. Q0 is valid. With default strict scheduling, Q7 is highest and Q0 lowest; no minimum bandwidth is guaranteed."
msgstr ""

msgid "QoS configuration saved. Changes take effect on reboot."
msgstr ""

msgid "The base mapping is unavailable. Update the QoS controller and refresh this page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Unknown base mapping: %s"
msgstr ""

msgid "Base mapping: original PPE compatibility map (ppe-legacy-v1). Empty overrides still use all 64 entries below. This is not a standard DiffServ or WMM mapping."
msgstr ""

msgid "This older configuration inherits ppe-legacy-v1. Saving makes the preset explicit without changing its mapping."
msgstr ""

