msgid "Traffic marking rules"
msgstr ""

msgid "Traffic to DSCP classification is configured in the firewall or another marking tool. After changing those rules, reboot the device so software and hardware offloaded flows learn the new marks. This page only defers its own hardware settings; an external rule editor may apply changes immediately."
msgstr ""

msgid "QoS configuration saved for the next device boot. Use System → Reboot when ready to apply it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configure traffic-to-DSCP rules in Firewall → Traffic Rules and describe their purpose in each rule name. A full firewall reload rebuilds its software and hardware flowtables. Updating a separate nft marking table alone does not retire old flows. Supported multicast firmware also retires its own cache through the firewall include. None of these actions applies a pending hardware mode or queue-map change."
msgstr ""

